<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African July retail trade sales down 0.5 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>S.African July retail trade sales down 0.5 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African retail trade sales fell a seasonally adjusted 0.5 percent month-on-month in July to 11.13 billion rand, latest Central Statistical Service (CSS) data shows.</p>
<p>Year-on-year, seasonally adjusted retail sales were up 9.8 percent from 10.13 billion rand in July 1995, the CSS said.</p>
<p>On an actual basis, retail trade sales were down 1.3 percent month-on-month and up 9.7 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Retail trade sales at current prices.</p>
<p>(rand million):</p>
<p>				 Jul '96	 Jun '96	Jul '95</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted  11,127.7	11,188.5     10,130.5</p>
<p>    Actual		   10,739.9	10,882.8	9,794.5</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
